## 13. Verification and acceptance

### Automated tests required in the delivered repository

Test the parts that can actually be established without the physical lamp:

- Pin assignments remain GPIO4/5/6 and are not overridden by example board support.
- Frame encoding, both polarity profiles, exact off/full-on, intermediate PWM rounding, LEDOUT packing, and readback masks.
- Discovery distinguishes an individual address from an all-call alias; ambiguous candidates do not trigger broadcast writes.
- Unused outputs remain off; warm/cool masks cannot overlap or exceed 16 channels.
- Preset math preserves the duty budget; default presets are pure warm and pure cool.
- All transitions in section 8, inactive OFF behavior, toggles, idempotent ON, serialized competing requests, and reconciliation recursion protection.
- Missing/corrupt configuration, canceled setup, interrupted save, reset scopes, and configuration import validation.
- Pulse expiry, abort, host disconnect, timer/control-thread ordering, and bounded I²C failure handling.
- Reboot starts off; a stale stored Matter on-state cannot illuminate the lamp during application initialization.
- Full image and partition layout fit the detected/declared flash capacity; clean reproducible build succeeds.

Use real assertions and a mock transport recording I²C transactions. Merely compiling or asserting `true` does not test these requirements.

### One installation acceptance session on the actual lamp

The provided host tool and README must make it straightforward to verify:

1. USB communication and correct chip/flash identification.
2. Individual address, verified off profile, and every used warm/cool channel.
3. Warm, Cool, and Off at the selected fixed brightness, with the two Matter endpoint states agreeing with the lamp.
4. Commissioning, commands from the intended controller, power-cycle persistence, reconnect after AP loss, and calibration retention through a Matter-only reset.
5. No persistent brownout/reset loop during commissioning or normal Wi-Fi use; measured memory statistics recorded.
